<MainLayout title="About Us" description="About Research.BetterHealthFacts.com – evidence-based health research and practical insights.">

  <h1>About Research.BetterHealthFacts.com</h1>

  <p>
    Research.BetterHealthFacts.com is the research-focused extension of BetterHealthFacts.com. 
    While the main site covers practical everyday health topics, this subdomain goes deeper into 
    the science behind common bodily experiences, symptoms, and modern lifestyle mismatches.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Focus On</h2>
  <p>
    We explore why certain sensations, patterns, and health issues are so common in modern life — 
    from everyday symptoms people often wonder about, to the evolutionary and physiological 
    reasons behind them. Our goal is to make complex research understandable without 
    oversimplifying it.
  </p>

  <h2>Our Approach</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clear explanations grounded in published research and established physiology</li>
    <li>Practical context that helps readers understand what is normal versus what needs attention</li>
    <li>A calm, evidence-informed tone rather than alarm or hype</li>
    <li>Topics chosen around real questions people search for in daily life</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Connection to BetterHealthFacts.com</h2>
  <p>
    This research subdomain works alongside the main BetterHealthFacts.com website. 
    Together, they aim to provide both accessible health information and deeper scientific context.
  </p>

  <h2>Important Note</h2>
  <p>
    The content on this site is for educational and informational purposes only. 
    It is not medical advice and should not replace consultation with a qualified healthcare professional.
  </p>

</MainLayout>